WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.230
“Come to me.” With those powerful words,

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:10.270
Jesus offered an invitation.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.130
He opened a door, or more than that,

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:18.790
he became the door into the life
our hearts have always longed for.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.750
A life made right-side up.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:25.110
A life lived in real
relationship with God.

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:28.770
Jesus did not only tell
us about that life,

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:31.370
he showed us what it looks like.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.970
He invited us to come to him,

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:38.710
learn from him and become fully alive.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.810
This is the hope at the
heart of every church,

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:47.230
that we would encourage one
another along this Jesus Journey.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:53.370
As our beliefs, our experience and
our everyday practices become more

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.930
aligned with the life of Jesus,

00:00:55.310 --> 00:01:00.630
we enjoy more of the relationship
with God that Jesus so clearly knew.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:05.510
But every church eventually
encounters an important question.

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:08.410
Where are we now?

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:12.230
Anyone who has hiked
into pristine backcountry

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.170
understands why that matters.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.670
We would not think of heading
off without a trail map.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.930
But before we can even begin using the map

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.490
to get to where we want to go,

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:27.110
we first need to know
where we are on that map.

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.530
Only then can we plot the journey.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.590
“You are here.”

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.350
Yet, when it comes to
becoming more like Jesus,

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:42.290
that starting point is often missing.

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:46.370
We can measure attendance,
programs and many other

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:47.630
signs of church activity.

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:53.130
Those things matter, but they do
not necessarily tell us where we

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.950
are in the deeper journey
of becoming like Jesus.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:00.570
And when we cannot see where we are,

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:04.830
it's easy to focus on improving
church structures and programs,

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:08.330
hoping they will somehow
produce deeper transformation.

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:11.730
We are often disappointed.

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:16.150
This is what the Jesus Journey is for.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:21.850
It helps individuals and churches
see more clearly where they are

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:24.630
now in their journey of
becoming more like Jesus.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:28.450
It takes the life of
Jesus as our true north,

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:32.810
what he believed, what he
experienced and how he lived in

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.050
relationship with his Father.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:38.550
Then, it helps us reflect
honestly on our own

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.390
beliefs, experiences and practices.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:44.770
This is not about being judged.

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:47.490
This is not about being compared.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:52.370
It is about discovering where
Jesus is already meeting us.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:57.710
Right where we are is the
edge of his invitation.

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:04.130
From there, he calls us forward
to trust him more deeply,

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.570
to experience more of his presence,

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:11.130
to reflect his character
and to serve in his way.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:15.670
Seeing where we are helps
us embrace the invitation

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.470
and the adventure ahead.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.770
Welcome to the Jesus Journey.
